## Summary

This PR implements the first, non-breaking step of the [`tool:` protocol RFC](https://github.com/pnpm/rfcs/pull/37). pnpm v12 now accepts `tool:` anywhere it accepts `runtime:` today, and `runtime:` keeps working as an alias:

- the Node.js, Bun, Deno, and Yarn 6 resolvers;
- `pnpm add` and `pnpm update`;
- `pnx node@tool:22`, `pnx bun@tool:1.3`, and `pnx yarn@tool:4`, plus `pnpm add -g yarn@tool:4`. `yarn@tool:<range>` maps to its Yarn line (npm `yarn`, `@yarnpkg/cli-dist`, or the native releases) the same way `yarn@<range>` does;
- folding into `devEngines.runtime` / `engines.runtime` when the manifest is written, and the `onFail` override;
- global shims, deploy, and the catalog-mode exemption;
- lockfile freshness. `tool:<spec>` and `runtime:<spec>` count as equal in both directions, so a frozen install accepts either spelling against a lockfile written with the other;
- the check that decides whether a locked version can be reused.

pnpm writes `runtime:` wherever it writes a specifier. `pnpm add node@tool:24` folds the entry into `devEngines.runtime` / `engines.runtime`, which store no protocol and read back as `runtime:<version>`, so the lockfile's importer specifier is `runtime:` too. A project that moves to `tool:` through pnpm commands therefore keeps a lockfile earlier pnpm versions accept with `--frozen-lockfile`.

